<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Çandarlı Halil Pasha the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1453">1453</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Çandarlı Halil Pasha, Halil Pasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Çandarlı Halil Pasha the Younger was grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from 1439 to 1453, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> and in the first years of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>, the fourth of the Çandarlı family to hold the office. When Murad abdicated in favour of the young Mehmed in 1444, and again during the Buçuktepe rebellion of 1446, Halil Pasha brought Murad back to the throne, which left Mehmed with a lasting resentment. He opposed the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and was suspected of taking bribes from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>. After the city fell on 29 May 1453, Mehmed had him imprisoned and executed on 10 July, the first Ottoman grand vizier to be executed by a sultan.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Mehmed II had his grand vizier <b>Çandarlı Halil Pasha</b> executed in 1453, these posts went more and more to the sultan’s kul, his “slaves”: boys taken from Christian families by the devshirme, converted to Islam and trained in the palace school, some 300 of them inside Topkapı…</blockquote><a href="/societies/ottoman-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Ottoman Empire</a></li></ul></section>
